WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.500
My name is Hogan Winklemann,

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.670
founder of the company called Travelping.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:10.070
We are entirely focused
on network services

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:13.839
and operator services,
developing software for that,

00:00:13.839 --> 00:00:15.620
for many, many years now.

00:00:15.620 --> 00:00:20.518
We have the advantage that
the network services we use,

00:00:20.518 --> 00:00:25.518
which are doing different
things, and just IT services,

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.310
they need to communicate to each other,

00:00:27.310 --> 00:00:30.710
and IBM Cloud was the only
platform we can find these days

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:35.710
where we can deploy such
horizontal services in the cloud.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.340
What it means for the
consumer is more speed,

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:42.560
faster downloads, bigger videos, etc.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.890
But this is not the
challenge for the carrier.

00:00:44.890 --> 00:00:47.210
The challenge for the
carrier are other use cases

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:50.135
like making a car
communicating to another car

00:00:50.135 --> 00:00:55.070
in sub-milliseconds to avoid an accident.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.700
This needs totally different deployment,

00:00:57.700 --> 00:01:00.170
architectures, and topologies,

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:02.600
which cannot be solved

00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:04.830
by just running a new software release.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:07.240
So, we need to create

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:11.090
another infrastructure for telco services,

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:13.370
which needs to go into the field

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:15.270
and which needs to be distributed.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:17.030
The Cloud is the foundation for that.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:22.030
So, you don't need to start
to mount telco equipment

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.790
in own data centers anymore

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:27.290
because 90% of the stack
is available in the Cloud.

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:30.000
You can use resources
wherever you want to go.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.610
This is one of the huge
advantages that global carriers,

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:36.504
or the local carriers can act globally,

00:01:36.504 --> 00:01:40.331
but fulfilling the local regulations.

00:01:40.331 --> 00:01:43.470
And because a company from Germany

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.220
can deploy in South Korea,

00:01:45.220 --> 00:01:48.690
which is one example we
have done on IBM Cloud.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:53.690
And deploying the service
last year in South Korea

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:57.010
was about talking to IMB engineers,

00:01:57.010 --> 00:02:00.070
fixing some networking problems for us

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:02.670
and this first, was a great experience.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:06.620
It's not just an API, it's
also API with a human.

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:10.060
With people helping you
if it's really required.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:10.893
Just was great.

00:02:10.893 --> 00:02:12.120
A major experience,

00:02:12.120 --> 00:02:13.693
and we got a service we need.

